  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday morning through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 229 PM EDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nBy Thu night the cold front that stalled across South GA will still \nbe in place with drier airmass across North and Central GA. The \nextended periods start off warm and dry Friday, but things begin to \nchange Sat. HIgh Temps Fri will still be in the upper 80s and 90s \nacross the area but with RH values in the 30-40% range it will not \nfell as humid and sticky as we have see the past few days. \n\nFri morning a closed low center begins to deepen over KS as it pushes \ninto MO Fri afternoon/evening. Its trailing cold front pushes \nthrough the Mid /southern MS river valley Fri night and begins \nknocking on NW GAs doorstep just before day break Sat. By Sat \nmorning The main low pressure center moves NE into the central Great \nlake states Sat and into the New England states Sun. The frontal \nboundary on the other hand stalls across E/SE GA and the Carolinas \nas a developing Bermuda ridge blocks it from moving off shore. With \nGA on the periphery of this Ridge it will keep us in moist SWLY \nflow through day 7. this will keep precipitation chances elevated \nwith a diurnally driven trend each day. With showers and \nthunderstorms expected each day day, highs temps will only get up \ninto the 80s to near 90 Sun/Mon/Tue.",
